window.REV_FLIP=window.REV_FLIP||{};window.REV_FLIP["kubernetes"]=[{"id":"kubernetes-f0001","card":"q-kubernetes-001-what-kubernetes-is-and-what-it-solves","sec":"kubernetes-s002","q":"What is Kubernetes, and why is it used?","a":"<p>Kubernetes (K8s) is an open-source platform for automating deployment, scaling, and management of containerized apps. It is used for scalability, resilience, and portability, handling load balancing, self-healing, and resource optimization across any environment.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0002","card":"q-kubernetes-001-what-kubernetes-is-and-what-it-solves","sec":"kubernetes-s002","q":"What problems does Kubernetes solve in container orchestration?","a":"<p>It automates deployment, scaling, load balancing, and self-healing. It manages resources, service discovery, and configs, and coordinates containers across multiple hosts for high availability.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0003","card":"q-kubernetes-001-what-kubernetes-is-and-what-it-solves","sec":"kubernetes-s002","q":"Explain the difference between Docker and Kubernetes.","a":"<p>Docker builds and runs containers on one host. Kubernetes orchestrates many containers across a cluster, adding scaling, scheduling, and networking.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0004","card":"q-kubernetes-001-what-kubernetes-is-and-what-it-solves","sec":"kubernetes-s002","q":"How does Kubernetes differ from traditional virtualization?","a":"<p>Containers share the host OS, which makes them lighter and faster than VMs that run full guest OSes. Kubernetes optimizes this for scale.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0005","card":"q-kubernetes-002-containers-clusters-and-nodes","sec":"kubernetes-s003","q":"What is a container, and how does Kubernetes manage containers?","a":"<p>A container is a lightweight, isolated app package with its dependencies. Kubernetes groups containers into Pods, schedules them on nodes, manages their lifecycle, and handles networking and scaling.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0006","card":"q-kubernetes-002-containers-clusters-and-nodes","sec":"kubernetes-s003","q":"What is the role of a Kubernetes cluster?","a":"<p>A group of nodes running containers, managed as one system for deployment, scaling, and fault tolerance.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0007","card":"q-kubernetes-002-containers-clusters-and-nodes","sec":"kubernetes-s003","q":"What is the difference between a node and a cluster?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Node</strong>: a single machine (master or worker).</li>\n  <li><strong>Cluster</strong>: all nodes working together under a control plane.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0008","card":"q-kubernetes-002-containers-clusters-and-nodes","sec":"kubernetes-s003","q":"What is a Pod in Kubernetes?","a":"<p>The smallest unit. It runs one or more containers that share network (IP) and storage. Pods are ephemeral and managed by controllers.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0009","card":"q-kubernetes-002-containers-clusters-and-nodes","sec":"kubernetes-s003","q":"What is a Namespace, and how is it used?","a":"<p>A logical partition that isolates resources, scopes access, and limits quotas for teams or projects.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0010","card":"q-kubernetes-003-control-plane-and-worker-node-components","sec":"kubernetes-s004","q":"What are the key components of Kubernetes architecture?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Control Plane</strong>: kube-apiserver, etcd, kube-scheduler, kube-controller-manager.</li>\n  <li><strong>Worker Nodes</strong>: kubelet, kube-proxy, container runtime (for example Docker).</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0011","card":"q-kubernetes-003-control-plane-and-worker-node-components","sec":"kubernetes-s004","q":"What is a control plane, and what does it consist of?","a":"<p>The brain of the cluster. It manages state and scheduling and includes kube-apiserver, etcd, kube-scheduler, and kube-controller-manager.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0012","card":"q-kubernetes-003-control-plane-and-worker-node-components","sec":"kubernetes-s004","q":"Explain the difference between master nodes and worker nodes.","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Master</strong>: runs the control plane (manages the cluster).</li>\n  <li><strong>Worker</strong>: runs Pods (executes workloads).</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0013","card":"q-kubernetes-004-what-each-component-does","sec":"kubernetes-s005","q":"Explain the role of the kube-apiserver.","a":"<p>The central hub. It exposes the API, handles requests, authenticates and authorizes them, and updates etcd.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0014","card":"q-kubernetes-004-what-each-component-does","sec":"kubernetes-s005","q":"What does the kube-scheduler do?","a":"<p>It places Pods on nodes based on resources, policies, and constraints.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0015","card":"q-kubernetes-004-what-each-component-does","sec":"kubernetes-s005","q":"What is the purpose of the kube-controller-manager?","a":"<p>It runs controllers that keep the cluster state (for example replicas and nodes) as desired.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0016","card":"q-kubernetes-004-what-each-component-does","sec":"kubernetes-s005","q":"What is etcd, and why is it important?","a":"<p>A distributed store for cluster state. It is critical for consistency and control plane operations.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0017","card":"q-kubernetes-004-what-each-component-does","sec":"kubernetes-s005","q":"How does the kubelet work on a worker node?","a":"<p>It is the node agent. It starts and stops containers, ensures Pods run, and reports to the control plane.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0018","card":"q-kubernetes-004-what-each-component-does","sec":"kubernetes-s005","q":"What is the role of kube-proxy?","a":"<p>It manages networking. It sets up rules for Service IPs and load balances traffic to Pods, using iptables or IPVS.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0019","card":"q-kubernetes-004-what-each-component-does","sec":"kubernetes-s005","q":"What is the Cloud Controller Manager, and when is it used?","a":"<p>It links Kubernetes to cloud APIs for nodes, load balancers, and storage. It is used in cloud-hosted clusters.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0020","card":"q-kubernetes-004-what-each-component-does","sec":"kubernetes-s005","q":"How does Kubernetes ensure high availability of the control plane?","a":"<p>Multiple master nodes, replicated etcd, leader election, and load-balanced API servers.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0021","card":"q-kubernetes-005-creating-a-pod","sec":"kubernetes-s006","q":"How do you create a Pod in Kubernetes?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: v1\nkind: Pod\nmetadata:\n  name: nginx-pod\nspec:\n  containers:\n  - name: nginx\n    image: nginx:latest\n    ports:\n    - containerPort: 80</code></pre></div>\n<p>Apply it with <code>kubectl apply -f pod.yaml</code>, or run it directly with <code>kubectl run my-pod --image=nginx --restart=Never</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0022","card":"q-kubernetes-006-pod-replicaset-and-deployment","sec":"kubernetes-s007","q":"What is the difference between a Pod and a Deployment?","a":"<p>A Pod is a single instance of containers. A Deployment manages Pods with replicas, updates, and self-healing.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0023","card":"q-kubernetes-006-pod-replicaset-and-deployment","sec":"kubernetes-s007","q":"What is a ReplicaSet, and how does it relate to a Deployment?","a":"<p>A ReplicaSet ensures a set number of Pods run. A Deployment creates and updates ReplicaSets for rollouts.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0024","card":"q-kubernetes-006-pod-replicaset-and-deployment","sec":"kubernetes-s007","q":"Explain the lifecycle of a Pod.","a":"<p><code>Pending → Running → Succeeded/Failed → (Unknown if lost)</code>. It is managed through init containers and probes.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0025","card":"q-kubernetes-006-pod-replicaset-and-deployment","sec":"kubernetes-s007","q":"What are labels and selectors, and how are they used?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Labels</strong>: key-value tags (for example <code>app=nginx</code>).</li>\n  <li><strong>Selectors</strong>: filter objects by labels for routing or management.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0026","card":"q-kubernetes-007-multi-container-pods-and-restarts","sec":"kubernetes-s008","q":"What is a multi-container Pod, and when would you use one?","a":"<p>Multiple containers in one Pod, used for sidecars (for example logging) or tightly coupled apps.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0027","card":"q-kubernetes-007-multi-container-pods-and-restarts","sec":"kubernetes-s008","q":"How do you restart a Pod without deleting it?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>For a Deployment: <code>kubectl rollout restart deployment &lt;name&gt;</code></li>\n  <li>Direct: edit the spec (for example add a label) or let probes fail.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0028","card":"q-kubernetes-008-statefulset-daemonset-job-and-cronjob","sec":"kubernetes-s009","q":"What is a StatefulSet, and how does it differ from a Deployment?","a":"<p>It manages stateful apps with stable names and storage. Unlike a Deployment, it is ordered and persistent.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0029","card":"q-kubernetes-008-statefulset-daemonset-job-and-cronjob","sec":"kubernetes-s009","q":"What is a DaemonSet, and when is it useful?","a":"<p>It runs one Pod per node, which suits monitoring, logging, or network agents.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0030","card":"q-kubernetes-008-statefulset-daemonset-job-and-cronjob","sec":"kubernetes-s009","q":"What is a Job and a CronJob?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Job</strong>: a one-time task that runs to completion.</li>\n  <li><strong>CronJob</strong>: scheduled Jobs (for example backups).</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0031","card":"q-kubernetes-009-how-pods-and-services-communicate","sec":"kubernetes-s010","q":"How does networking work in Kubernetes?","a":"<p>Pods get unique IPs, communicate over a flat network (CNI), and use Services for stable access.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0032","card":"q-kubernetes-009-how-pods-and-services-communicate","sec":"kubernetes-s010","q":"How do Pods communicate with each other?","a":"<p>By direct IP or through a Service ClusterIP, enabled by CNI and DNS.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0033","card":"q-kubernetes-009-how-pods-and-services-communicate","sec":"kubernetes-s010","q":"What is a CNI (Container Network Interface), and why is it important?","a":"<p>The standard for Pod networking. It assigns IPs and routes traffic (for example Flannel, Calico).</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0034","card":"q-kubernetes-009-how-pods-and-services-communicate","sec":"kubernetes-s010","q":"How does Kubernetes handle DNS resolution within a cluster?","a":"<p>CoreDNS assigns names like <code>&lt;service&gt;.&lt;namespace&gt;.svc.cluster.local</code> for Pod and Service discovery.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0035","card":"q-kubernetes-010-service-types","sec":"kubernetes-s011","q":"What is a ClusterIP service, and how does it work?","a":"<p>The default Service type. It gives a virtual IP for internal Pod access, load balanced by kube-proxy.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0036","card":"q-kubernetes-010-service-types","sec":"kubernetes-s011","q":"Explain the difference between ClusterIP, NodePort, and LoadBalancer.","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>ClusterIP</strong>: internal only.</li>\n  <li><strong>NodePort</strong>: exposes on node ports (30000-32767).</li>\n  <li><strong>LoadBalancer</strong>: external IP from the cloud.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0037","card":"q-kubernetes-010-service-types","sec":"kubernetes-s011","q":"How does Kubernetes handle external traffic to services?","a":"<p>Through NodePort (node IP:port), LoadBalancer (cloud IP), or Ingress (HTTP routing).</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0038","card":"q-kubernetes-010-service-types","sec":"kubernetes-s011","q":"What is an Ingress controller, and why is it used?","a":"<p>It manages HTTP traffic. It routes by host and path, handles TLS, and cuts LoadBalancer costs.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0039","card":"q-kubernetes-010-service-types","sec":"kubernetes-s011","q":"What is the purpose of kube-proxy in networking?","a":"<p>It sets up Service IPs and load balances traffic to Pods using iptables or IPVS.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0040","card":"q-kubernetes-011-network-policy","sec":"kubernetes-s012","q":"What is a Network Policy, and how can you enforce it?","a":"<p>Rules that control Pod traffic. They are enforced by CNI plugins such as Calico.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0041","card":"q-kubernetes-012-pv-pvc-and-storageclass","sec":"kubernetes-s013","q":"What is a Persistent Volume (PV)?","a":"<p>A cluster storage resource that abstracts disks (for example NFS or cloud disks) for Pods.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0042","card":"q-kubernetes-012-pv-pvc-and-storageclass","sec":"kubernetes-s013","q":"What is a Persistent Volume Claim (PVC), and how does it relate to a PV?","a":"<p>A user request for storage. It binds to a matching PV for Pod use.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0043","card":"q-kubernetes-012-pv-pvc-and-storageclass","sec":"kubernetes-s013","q":"Explain static vs dynamic provisioning.","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Static</strong>: an admin pre-creates PVs.</li>\n  <li><strong>Dynamic</strong>: PVs are created on demand through a StorageClass.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0044","card":"q-kubernetes-012-pv-pvc-and-storageclass","sec":"kubernetes-s013","q":"What is a StorageClass, and how does it work?","a":"<p>It defines storage types (for example SSD) for dynamic PV provisioning.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0045","card":"q-kubernetes-013-access-modes-csi-and-reclaim-policy","sec":"kubernetes-s014","q":"What are the access modes for Persistent Volumes?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>RWO</strong>: read-write, one node.</li>\n  <li><strong>ROX</strong>: read-only, many nodes.</li>\n  <li><strong>RWX</strong>: read-write, many nodes.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0046","card":"q-kubernetes-013-access-modes-csi-and-reclaim-policy","sec":"kubernetes-s014","q":"How does Kubernetes handle storage in a multi-node cluster?","a":"<p>It uses PV/PVC with node affinity (RWO) or shared systems (RWX) through CSI.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0047","card":"q-kubernetes-013-access-modes-csi-and-reclaim-policy","sec":"kubernetes-s014","q":"What is the role of CSI (Container Storage Interface)?","a":"<p>It standardizes storage drivers and enables dynamic provisioning and advanced features.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0048","card":"q-kubernetes-013-access-modes-csi-and-reclaim-policy","sec":"kubernetes-s014","q":"What happens to a PV when a PVC is deleted?","a":"<p>It depends on the reclaim policy: Retain (keeps the PV), Delete (removes the PV), or Recycle (wipes the data).</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0049","card":"q-kubernetes-014-attaching-storage-and-troubleshooting","sec":"kubernetes-s015","q":"How do you attach storage to a Pod?","a":"<p>Reference the PVC under <code>volumes</code> and mount it in the container.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>volumes:\n- name: my-volume\n  persistentVolumeClaim:\n    claimName: my-pvc</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0050","card":"q-kubernetes-014-attaching-storage-and-troubleshooting","sec":"kubernetes-s015","q":"How do you troubleshoot storage issues?","a":"<p>Check Pod events (<code>kubectl describe</code>), PVC/PV binding, and StorageClass config.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0051","card":"q-kubernetes-015-configmaps-and-secrets","sec":"kubernetes-s016","q":"What is a ConfigMap, and how is it used?","a":"<p>It stores non-sensitive config data, used as env vars or files in Pods.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0052","card":"q-kubernetes-015-configmaps-and-secrets","sec":"kubernetes-s016","q":"What is a Secret, and how does it differ from a ConfigMap?","a":"<p>A Secret stores sensitive data (for example passwords) and is base64-encoded. A ConfigMap holds plain text.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0053","card":"q-kubernetes-015-configmaps-and-secrets","sec":"kubernetes-s016","q":"What is the difference between a base64-encoded Secret and a plain-text ConfigMap?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Secret</strong>: encoded for obscurity.</li>\n  <li><strong>ConfigMap</strong>: raw text for configs.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0054","card":"q-kubernetes-015-configmaps-and-secrets","sec":"kubernetes-s016","q":"How do you create and manage Secrets?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kubectl create secret generic my-secret --from-literal=key=value</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0055","card":"q-kubernetes-016-injecting-values-into-pods","sec":"kubernetes-s017","q":"How do you inject environment variables into a Pod?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>env:\n- name: ENV_VAR\n  value: &quot;value&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0056","card":"q-kubernetes-016-injecting-values-into-pods","sec":"kubernetes-s017","q":"How do you pass sensitive data to an application?","a":"<p>Use Secrets as env vars or mounted files.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0057","card":"q-kubernetes-016-injecting-values-into-pods","sec":"kubernetes-s017","q":"How can you mount a ConfigMap or Secret as a volume?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>volumes:\n- name: config-vol\n  configMap:\n    name: my-config</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0058","card":"q-kubernetes-016-injecting-values-into-pods","sec":"kubernetes-s017","q":"How do you update a ConfigMap or Secret without restarting a Pod?","a":"<p>Mount it as a volume. The Pod sees updates automatically, with some delay.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0059","card":"q-kubernetes-017-securing-secrets","sec":"kubernetes-s018","q":"What are the security best practices for managing Secrets?","a":"<p>Encrypt at rest, use RBAC, avoid logging, and rotate regularly.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0060","card":"q-kubernetes-017-securing-secrets","sec":"kubernetes-s018","q":"What is the role of RBAC in securing ConfigMaps and Secrets?","a":"<p>It restricts who can read or write them via Roles and Bindings.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0061","card":"q-kubernetes-018-how-the-scheduler-places-pods","sec":"kubernetes-s019","q":"How does the scheduler decide where to place a Pod?","a":"<p>It filters nodes (resources, taints), then scores them based on policies (for example least usage).</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0062","card":"q-kubernetes-018-how-the-scheduler-places-pods","sec":"kubernetes-s019","q":"What is a node selector, and how does it work?","a":"<p>It matches Pods to nodes by labels (for example <code>nodeSelector: disk=ssd</code>).</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0063","card":"q-kubernetes-018-how-the-scheduler-places-pods","sec":"kubernetes-s019","q":"What is a taint and toleration, and how are they used?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Taint</strong>: repels Pods from nodes.</li>\n  <li><strong>Toleration</strong>: allows Pods to ignore taints.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Taint a node and tolerate it in a Pod:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kubectl taint nodes &lt;node&gt; app=backend:NoSchedule</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>tolerations:\n- key: &quot;app&quot;\n  operator: &quot;Equal&quot;\n  value: &quot;backend&quot;\n  effect: &quot;NoSchedule&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0064","card":"q-kubernetes-019-requests-and-limits","sec":"kubernetes-s020","q":"What are resource requests and limits?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Requests</strong>: the minimum needed.</li>\n  <li><strong>Limits</strong>: the maximum allowed (CPU/memory).</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>spec:\n  containers:\n  - name: nginx\n    image: nginx\n    resources:\n      requests:\n        cpu: &quot;250m&quot;\n        memory: &quot;64Mi&quot;\n      limits:\n        cpu: &quot;500m&quot;\n        memory: &quot;128Mi&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0065","card":"q-kubernetes-019-requests-and-limits","sec":"kubernetes-s020","q":"What happens when a Pod exceeds its resource limits?","a":"<p>CPU is throttled and memory causes an OOM kill.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0066","card":"q-kubernetes-019-requests-and-limits","sec":"kubernetes-s020","q":"What is a Quality of Service (QoS) class, and how is it assigned?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Guaranteed</strong>: limits = requests.</li>\n  <li><strong>Burstable</strong>: requests &lt; limits.</li>\n  <li><strong>BestEffort</strong>: none set. Assigned automatically.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0067","card":"q-kubernetes-020-priority-and-eviction","sec":"kubernetes-s021","q":"How do you prioritize Pods, and what is a PriorityClass?","a":"<p>Use a PriorityClass. Higher priority Pods get scheduled first.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: scheduling.k8s.io/v1\nkind: PriorityClass\nmetadata:\n  name: high-priority\nvalue: 1000</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0068","card":"q-kubernetes-020-priority-and-eviction","sec":"kubernetes-s021","q":"How does Kubernetes handle Pod eviction?","a":"<p>It evicts low-priority or over-limit Pods when resources are tight.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0069","card":"q-kubernetes-020-priority-and-eviction","sec":"kubernetes-s021","q":"How do you troubleshoot a Pod stuck in Pending?","a":"<p>Check events (<code>kubectl describe</code>), resources, taints, and PVCs.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0070","card":"q-kubernetes-021-autoscaling","sec":"kubernetes-s022","q":"What is Horizontal Pod Autoscaling (HPA), and how does it work?","a":"<p>It scales Pod replicas based on CPU or memory and needs the metrics server.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0071","card":"q-kubernetes-021-autoscaling","sec":"kubernetes-s022","q":"How do you configure HPA based on custom metrics?","a":"<p>Use Prometheus Adapter and set the custom metric target in the HPA spec.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0072","card":"q-kubernetes-021-autoscaling","sec":"kubernetes-s022","q":"What is Vertical Pod Autoscaling (VPA), and when is it useful?","a":"<p>It adjusts Pod resource limits, which helps optimize fixed workloads.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0073","card":"q-kubernetes-021-autoscaling","sec":"kubernetes-s022","q":"How do you scale an application for sudden traffic spikes?","a":"<p>Use HPA or scale manually with <code>kubectl scale</code>, plus the cluster autoscaler.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0074","card":"q-kubernetes-022-updates-and-failover","sec":"kubernetes-s023","q":"How does Kubernetes ensure high availability of applications?","a":"<p>Through replicas, multi-node scheduling, and self-healing via controllers.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0075","card":"q-kubernetes-022-updates-and-failover","sec":"kubernetes-s023","q":"What is a rolling update, and how do you perform one?","a":"<p>Gradual Pod replacement: <code>kubectl set image deployment/&lt;name&gt; container=new-image</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0076","card":"q-kubernetes-022-updates-and-failover","sec":"kubernetes-s023","q":"What is the difference between a rolling update and a recreate strategy?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Rolling</strong>: zero downtime, gradual.</li>\n  <li><strong>Recreate</strong>: kills all Pods, then restarts them.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0077","card":"q-kubernetes-022-updates-and-failover","sec":"kubernetes-s023","q":"How does Kubernetes handle failover for Pods?","a":"<p>Controllers (for example a Deployment) reschedule failed Pods to healthy nodes.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0078","card":"q-kubernetes-023-liveness-and-readiness-probes","sec":"kubernetes-s024","q":"What is the role of liveness and readiness probes?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Liveness</strong>: restarts unhealthy Pods.</li>\n  <li><strong>Readiness</strong>: controls whether the Pod receives traffic.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0079","card":"q-kubernetes-023-liveness-and-readiness-probes","sec":"kubernetes-s024","q":"How do you configure liveness and readiness probes?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>livenessProbe:\n  httpGet:\n    path: /health\n    port: 80\n  initialDelaySeconds: 5\nreadinessProbe:\n  httpGet:\n    path: /ready\n    port: 80</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0080","card":"q-kubernetes-023-liveness-and-readiness-probes","sec":"kubernetes-s024","q":"What happens if a readiness probe fails?","a":"<p>The Pod is marked NotReady and traffic stops until the probe passes.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0081","card":"q-kubernetes-024-rbac-roles-and-serviceaccounts","sec":"kubernetes-s025","q":"What is Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)?","a":"<p>It controls permissions by linking Roles and ClusterRoles to users through Bindings.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0082","card":"q-kubernetes-024-rbac-roles-and-serviceaccounts","sec":"kubernetes-s025","q":"What is the difference between a ClusterRole and a Role?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>ClusterRole</strong>: cluster-wide permissions.</li>\n  <li><strong>Role</strong>: namespace-specific permissions.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0083","card":"q-kubernetes-024-rbac-roles-and-serviceaccounts","sec":"kubernetes-s025","q":"What is a ServiceAccount, and how is it used?","a":"<p>It is an identity for Pods and provides an API token for app access.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0084","card":"q-kubernetes-024-rbac-roles-and-serviceaccounts","sec":"kubernetes-s025","q":"How do you create a Role and a RoleBinding?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1\nkind: Role\nmetadata:\n  name: pod-reader\nrules:\n- apiGroups: [&quot;&quot;]\n  resources: [&quot;pods&quot;]\n  verbs: [&quot;get&quot;, &quot;list&quot;]\n---\napiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1\nkind: RoleBinding\nmetadata:\n  name: read-pods\nsubjects:\n- kind: User\n  name: &quot;user1&quot;\nroleRef:\n  kind: Role\n  name: pod-reader\n  apiGroup: rbac.authorization.k8s.io</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0085","card":"q-kubernetes-025-authentication-authorization-and-hardeni","sec":"kubernetes-s026","q":"How does Kubernetes handle authentication and authorization?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Authentication</strong>: certs, tokens, OIDC.</li>\n  <li><strong>Authorization</strong>: RBAC, ABAC, or webhooks.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0086","card":"q-kubernetes-025-authentication-authorization-and-hardeni","sec":"kubernetes-s026","q":"How do you secure the API server?","a":"<p>Use TLS and RBAC, disable anonymous access, and restrict network access.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0087","card":"q-kubernetes-025-authentication-authorization-and-hardeni","sec":"kubernetes-s026","q":"What are Pod Security Policies (PSPs)?","a":"<p>They enforce Pod security rules (for example no root access). PSPs are deprecated in favor of Pod Security Admission (PSA).</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0088","card":"q-kubernetes-025-authentication-authorization-and-hardeni","sec":"kubernetes-s026","q":"What are some best practices for securing a cluster?","a":"<p>Use RBAC and TLS, encrypt Secrets, limit privileges, and enable audit logs.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0089","card":"q-kubernetes-025-authentication-authorization-and-hardeni","sec":"kubernetes-s026","q":"How do you audit and monitor security events?","a":"<p>Enable API audit logs and use tools like Prometheus or Falco.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0090","card":"q-kubernetes-026-restricting-traffic-with-network-policie","sec":"kubernetes-s027","q":"How do you restrict network traffic using Network Policies?","a":"<p>Select the target Pods and list which Pods may reach them. This policy lets only <code>frontend</code> Pods reach <code>backend</code> Pods on port 80.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1\nkind: NetworkPolicy\nmetadata:\n  name: allow-specific\nspec:\n  podSelector:\n    matchLabels:\n      app: backend\n  ingress:\n  - from:\n    - podSelector:\n        matchLabels:\n          app: frontend\n    ports:\n    - protocol: TCP\n      port: 80</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0091","card":"q-kubernetes-027-inspecting-pods-and-logs","sec":"kubernetes-s028","q":"How do you check the status of Pods in a cluster?","a":"<p><code>kubectl get pods --all-namespaces -o wide</code></p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0092","card":"q-kubernetes-027-inspecting-pods-and-logs","sec":"kubernetes-s028","q":"What is the purpose of <code>kubectl describe</code>?","a":"<p>It shows detailed resource information and is useful for debugging events.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0093","card":"q-kubernetes-027-inspecting-pods-and-logs","sec":"kubernetes-s028","q":"How do you view logs of a Pod?","a":"<p><code>kubectl logs &lt;pod-name&gt; -c &lt;container&gt;</code></p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0094","card":"q-kubernetes-027-inspecting-pods-and-logs","sec":"kubernetes-s028","q":"What does <code>kubectl get events</code> do?","a":"<p>It lists cluster events, which helps identify issues.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0095","card":"q-kubernetes-028-debugging-failures","sec":"kubernetes-s029","q":"How do you debug a Pod that is crashing?","a":"<p>Check logs (<code>kubectl logs --previous</code>), events, and the Pod spec.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0096","card":"q-kubernetes-028-debugging-failures","sec":"kubernetes-s029","q":"What are common reasons for a Pod to be in CrashLoopBackOff?","a":"<p>Application errors, a bad image, resource limits, or probe failures.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0097","card":"q-kubernetes-028-debugging-failures","sec":"kubernetes-s029","q":"How do you troubleshoot a service that is not responding?","a":"<p>Check endpoints, Pods, and networking, and test with <code>kubectl port-forward</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0098","card":"q-kubernetes-029-metrics-and-dashboards","sec":"kubernetes-s030","q":"What is Prometheus, and how is it used with Kubernetes?","a":"<p>It monitors metrics by scraping cluster and app data for alerts and visualization.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0099","card":"q-kubernetes-029-metrics-and-dashboards","sec":"kubernetes-s030","q":"How do you monitor resource usage in a cluster?","a":"<p>Use <code>kubectl top</code>, Metrics Server, or Prometheus/Grafana.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0100","card":"q-kubernetes-029-metrics-and-dashboards","sec":"kubernetes-s030","q":"What is the Kubernetes Dashboard, and how do you access it?","a":"<p>A UI for cluster management, reached through <code>kubectl proxy</code> and a token.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0101","card":"q-kubernetes-030-deploying-from-pipelines","sec":"kubernetes-s031","q":"How do you integrate Kubernetes with a CI/CD pipeline?","a":"<p>Build and test in CI, then deploy via <code>kubectl apply</code> or Helm in CD.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0102","card":"q-kubernetes-030-deploying-from-pipelines","sec":"kubernetes-s031","q":"How do you automate deployments?","a":"<p>Use CI/CD pipelines, GitOps tools, or scripted <code>kubectl</code> commands.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0103","card":"q-kubernetes-030-deploying-from-pipelines","sec":"kubernetes-s031","q":"What is the difference between <code>kubectl apply</code> and <code>kubectl create</code>?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Apply</strong>: declarative, updates existing resources.</li>\n  <li><strong>Create</strong>: imperative, creates a resource once.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0104","card":"q-kubernetes-030-deploying-from-pipelines","sec":"kubernetes-s031","q":"How do you roll back a deployment?","a":"<p><code>kubectl rollout undo deployment/&lt;name&gt;</code></p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0105","card":"q-kubernetes-030-deploying-from-pipelines","sec":"kubernetes-s031","q":"How do you manage multiple environments (dev, staging, prod)?","a":"<p>Use Namespaces, ConfigMaps, Helm values, or Kustomize overlays.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0106","card":"q-kubernetes-031-gitops","sec":"kubernetes-s032","q":"What is GitOps, and how does it work with Kubernetes?","a":"<p>Git is the source of truth, and tools sync manifests to the cluster automatically.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0107","card":"q-kubernetes-031-gitops","sec":"kubernetes-s032","q":"How do you use ArgoCD or Flux?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>ArgoCD</strong>: UI-driven sync.</li>\n  <li><strong>Flux</strong>: lightweight Git watcher.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0108","card":"q-kubernetes-032-helm","sec":"kubernetes-s033","q":"What is Helm, and how does it simplify deployments?","a":"<p>A package manager that uses charts to templatize and deploy applications.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0109","card":"q-kubernetes-032-helm","sec":"kubernetes-s033","q":"What are Helm charts, and how do you create one?","a":"<p>Bundled manifests. Run <code>helm create &lt;name&gt;</code> and edit <code>values.yaml</code>.</p>\n<p>A simple web application chart has these files.</p>\n<p><code>Chart.yaml</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: v2\nname: nginx-chart\nversion: 0.1.0</code></pre></div>\n<p><code>values.yaml</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>replicaCount: 3\nimage:\n  repository: nginx\n  tag: latest\nservice:\n  type: LoadBalancer\n  port: 80</code></pre></div>\n<p><code>templates/deployment.yaml</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  name: {{ .Release.Name }}-nginx\nspec:\n  replicas: {{ .Values.replicaCount }}\n  selector:\n    matchLabels:\n      app: nginx\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      labels:\n        app: nginx\n    spec:\n      containers:\n      - name: nginx\n        image: {{ .Values.image.repository }}:{{ .Values.image.tag }}\n        ports:\n        - containerPort: 80</code></pre></div>\n<p><code>templates/service.yaml</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: v1\nkind: Service\nmetadata:\n  name: {{ .Release.Name }}-nginx-service\nspec:\n  selector:\n    app: nginx\n  ports:\n  - port: {{ .Values.service.port }}\n    targetPort: 80\n  type: {{ .Values.service.type }}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0110","card":"q-kubernetes-033-extending-kubernetes","sec":"kubernetes-s034","q":"What is a Custom Resource Definition (CRD)?","a":"<p>It extends the API with custom resources (for example MyApp).</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0111","card":"q-kubernetes-033-extending-kubernetes","sec":"kubernetes-s034","q":"How do you extend Kubernetes with custom controllers?","a":"<p>Write logic (for example in Go) that manages CRD instances.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0112","card":"q-kubernetes-033-extending-kubernetes","sec":"kubernetes-s034","q":"What is a Kubernetes operator, and how does it work?","a":"<p>A custom controller that manages an application's lifecycle via CRDs.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0113","card":"q-kubernetes-033-extending-kubernetes","sec":"kubernetes-s034","q":"What is a sidecar container, and how is it used?","a":"<p>A helper container in a Pod that adds logging, proxying, and similar functions.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0114","card":"q-kubernetes-034-platform-and-operations","sec":"kubernetes-s035","q":"How does Kubernetes handle multi-tenancy?","a":"<p>Namespaces, RBAC, and quotas. Isolation is limited without additional tools.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0115","card":"q-kubernetes-034-platform-and-operations","sec":"kubernetes-s035","q":"What is Federation, and when is it used?","a":"<p>It manages multiple clusters and is used for multi-region setups or disaster recovery.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0116","card":"q-kubernetes-034-platform-and-operations","sec":"kubernetes-s035","q":"How do you upgrade a cluster without downtime?","a":"<p>Do rolling upgrades of the control plane and nodes: drain, update, uncordon.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0117","card":"q-kubernetes-034-platform-and-operations","sec":"kubernetes-s035","q":"What is the difference between Kubernetes and OpenShift?","a":"<p>OpenShift is Kubernetes plus enterprise features (UI, CI/CD, security).</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0118","card":"q-kubernetes-034-platform-and-operations","sec":"kubernetes-s035","q":"How do you configure a cluster on a cloud provider?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>EKS</strong>: <code>eksctl create</code>.</li>\n  <li><strong>GKE</strong>: <code>gcloud container</code>.</li>\n  <li><strong>AKS</strong>: <code>az aks</code>.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0119","card":"q-kubernetes-034-platform-and-operations","sec":"kubernetes-s035","q":"What is KubeVirt, and how does it integrate VMs with Kubernetes?","a":"<p>It runs VMs as Pods, using CRDs and QEMU.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0120","card":"q-kubernetes-034-platform-and-operations","sec":"kubernetes-s035","q":"How does Kubernetes handle disaster recovery?","a":"<p>Back up etcd, replicate clusters, and use external storage.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0121","card":"q-kubernetes-035-pods-services-and-nodes","sec":"kubernetes-s036","q":"A Pod is stuck in Pending. How do you troubleshoot it?","a":"<p>Check resources, taints, and PVCs via <code>kubectl describe</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0122","card":"q-kubernetes-035-pods-services-and-nodes","sec":"kubernetes-s036","q":"A service is not accessible externally. What steps would you take?","a":"<p>Verify the service type, endpoints, Pods, and network rules.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0123","card":"q-kubernetes-035-pods-services-and-nodes","sec":"kubernetes-s036","q":"You notice high CPU usage in your cluster. How do you identify the cause?","a":"<p>Use <code>kubectl top</code>, logs, and Prometheus to find the culprits.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0124","card":"q-kubernetes-035-pods-services-and-nodes","sec":"kubernetes-s036","q":"How would you handle a node failure?","a":"<p>Drain the node, replace it, reschedule Pods, and scale if needed.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0125","card":"q-kubernetes-035-pods-services-and-nodes","sec":"kubernetes-s036","q":"A StatefulSet is not creating Pods as expected. What could be the issue?","a":"<p>Check PVC binding, resource limits, or a headless Service misconfiguration.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0126","card":"q-kubernetes-036-releases-migration-and-recovery","sec":"kubernetes-s037","q":"A deployment fails after an update. How do you roll it back?","a":"<p><code>kubectl rollout undo deployment/&lt;name&gt;</code></p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0127","card":"q-kubernetes-036-releases-migration-and-recovery","sec":"kubernetes-s037","q":"How do you migrate an application from a single server to Kubernetes?","a":"<p>Containerize it, define a Deployment and Service, move data, and cut over.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0128","card":"q-kubernetes-036-releases-migration-and-recovery","sec":"kubernetes-s037","q":"A Secret is accidentally exposed. What do you do?","a":"<p>Rotate the Secret, delete the old one, audit access, and encrypt etcd.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0129","card":"q-kubernetes-036-releases-migration-and-recovery","sec":"kubernetes-s037","q":"How do you recover a cluster if the etcd database is corrupted?","a":"<p>Restore from backup, restart the control plane, and verify.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0130","card":"q-kubernetes-037-exposing-a-deployment","sec":"kubernetes-s038","q":"Write a YAML file to create a Deployment with 3 replicas.","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  name: nginx-deployment\nspec:\n  replicas: 3\n  selector:\n    matchLabels:\n      app: nginx\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      labels:\n        app: nginx\n    spec:\n      containers:\n      - name: nginx\n        image: nginx:latest\n        ports:\n        - containerPort: 80</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0131","card":"q-kubernetes-037-exposing-a-deployment","sec":"kubernetes-s038","q":"How do you expose a Deployment as a LoadBalancer service?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: v1\nkind: Service\nmetadata:\n  name: nginx-service\nspec:\n  selector:\n    app: nginx\n  ports:\n  - port: 80\n    targetPort: 80\n  type: LoadBalancer</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0132","card":"q-kubernetes-038-services-and-configmaps","sec":"kubernetes-s039","q":"How do you create a Service to expose a Deployment?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: v1\nkind: Service\nmetadata:\n  name: my-service\nspec:\n  selector:\n    app: nginx\n  ports:\n  - protocol: TCP\n    port: 80\n    targetPort: 80\n  type: ClusterIP</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0133","card":"q-kubernetes-038-services-and-configmaps","sec":"kubernetes-s039","q":"How do you create a Service and a Pod it selects?","a":"<p>The Pod label must match the Service selector.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: v1\nkind: Service\nmetadata:\n  name: my-service\nspec:\n  selector:\n    app: my-app\n  ports:\n  - protocol: TCP\n    port: 80\n    targetPort: 80\n---\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Pod\nmetadata:\n  name: my-pod\n  labels:\n    app: my-app\nspec:\n  containers:\n  - name: nginx\n    image: nginx</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0134","card":"q-kubernetes-038-services-and-configmaps","sec":"kubernetes-s039","q":"How do you create a ConfigMap?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: v1\nkind: ConfigMap\nmetadata:\n  name: my-configmap\ndata:\n  key1: value1\n  key2: value2</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0135","card":"q-kubernetes-038-services-and-configmaps","sec":"kubernetes-s039","q":"How do you attach a ConfigMap to a Pod as an environment variable?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: v1\nkind: Pod\nmetadata:\n  name: my-pod-with-configmap\nspec:\n  containers:\n  - name: nginx\n    image: nginx\n    env:\n    - name: KEY1\n      valueFrom:\n        configMapKeyRef:\n          name: my-configmap\n          key: key1</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0136","card":"q-kubernetes-039-secrets","sec":"kubernetes-s040","q":"How do you create a Secret?","a":"<p>Values under <code>data</code> are base64-encoded.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: v1\nkind: Secret\nmetadata:\n  name: my-secret\ntype: Opaque\ndata:\n  username: YWRtaW4=   # base64 for &quot;admin&quot;\n  password: cGFzc3dvcmQ=   # base64 for &quot;password&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0137","card":"q-kubernetes-039-secrets","sec":"kubernetes-s040","q":"How do you attach a Secret to a Pod?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: v1\nkind: Pod\nmetadata:\n  name: my-pod-with-secret\nspec:\n  containers:\n  - name: nginx\n    image: nginx\n    env:\n    - name: USERNAME\n      valueFrom:\n        secretKeyRef:\n          name: my-secret\n          key: username</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0138","card":"q-kubernetes-039-secrets","sec":"kubernetes-s040","q":"How do you create a TLS Secret?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kubectl create secret tls tls-secret --key tls.key --cert tls.crt</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0139","card":"q-kubernetes-040-persistent-storage-manifests","sec":"kubernetes-s041","q":"How do you create a PersistentVolume (PV)?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: v1\nkind: PersistentVolume\nmetadata:\n  name: my-pv\nspec:\n  capacity:\n    storage: 1Gi\n  accessModes:\n  - ReadWriteOnce\n  hostPath:\n    path: /mnt/data</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0140","card":"q-kubernetes-040-persistent-storage-manifests","sec":"kubernetes-s041","q":"How do you create a PVC and attach it to a Pod?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: v1\nkind: PersistentVolumeClaim\nmetadata:\n  name: my-pvc\nspec:\n  accessModes:\n  - ReadWriteOnce\n  resources:\n    requests:\n      storage: 1Gi\n---\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Pod\nmetadata:\n  name: my-pod-with-pvc\nspec:\n  containers:\n  - name: nginx\n    image: nginx\n    volumeMounts:\n    - mountPath: /data\n      name: my-volume\n  volumes:\n  - name: my-volume\n    persistentVolumeClaim:\n      claimName: my-pvc</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0141","card":"q-kubernetes-040-persistent-storage-manifests","sec":"kubernetes-s041","q":"How do you attach a PVC to a Deployment?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  name: my-deployment-with-pvc\nspec:\n  replicas: 1\n  selector:\n    matchLabels:\n      app: nginx\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      labels:\n        app: nginx\n    spec:\n      containers:\n      - name: nginx\n        image: nginx\n        volumeMounts:\n        - mountPath: /data\n          name: my-volume\n      volumes:\n      - name: my-volume\n        persistentVolumeClaim:\n          claimName: my-pvc</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0142","card":"q-kubernetes-040-persistent-storage-manifests","sec":"kubernetes-s041","q":"What is the YAML for a 10Gi PVC with a StorageClass?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: v1\nkind: PersistentVolumeClaim\nmetadata:\n  name: my-pvc\nspec:\n  accessModes: [ReadWriteOnce]\n  resources:\n    requests:\n      storage: 10Gi\n  storageClassName: standard</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0143","card":"q-kubernetes-041-workload-controllers","sec":"kubernetes-s042","q":"How do you create a ReplicaSet with 2 replicas?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: ReplicaSet\nmetadata:\n  name: my-replicaset\nspec:\n  replicas: 2\n  selector:\n    matchLabels:\n      app: nginx\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      labels:\n        app: nginx\n    spec:\n      containers:\n      - name: nginx\n        image: nginx</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0144","card":"q-kubernetes-041-workload-controllers","sec":"kubernetes-s042","q":"How do you create a StatefulSet with 2 replicas?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: StatefulSet\nmetadata:\n  name: my-statefulset\nspec:\n  serviceName: &quot;nginx&quot;\n  replicas: 2\n  selector:\n    matchLabels:\n      app: nginx\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      labels:\n        app: nginx\n    spec:\n      containers:\n      - name: nginx\n        image: nginx</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0145","card":"q-kubernetes-041-workload-controllers","sec":"kubernetes-s042","q":"How do you create a DaemonSet?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: DaemonSet\nmetadata:\n  name: my-daemonset\nspec:\n  selector:\n    matchLabels:\n      app: fluentd\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      labels:\n        app: fluentd\n    spec:\n      containers:\n      - name: fluentd\n        image: fluentd</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0146","card":"q-kubernetes-042-jobs-and-cronjobs","sec":"kubernetes-s043","q":"How do you create a Job?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: batch/v1\nkind: Job\nmetadata:\n  name: my-job\nspec:\n  template:\n    spec:\n      containers:\n      - name: pi\n        image: perl\n        command: [&quot;perl&quot;, &quot;-Mbignum=bpi&quot;, &quot;-wle&quot;, &quot;print bpi(2000)&quot;]\n      restartPolicy: Never</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0147","card":"q-kubernetes-042-jobs-and-cronjobs","sec":"kubernetes-s043","q":"How do you create a CronJob that echoes \"Hello\" every 5 minutes?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: batch/v1\nkind: CronJob\nmetadata:\n  name: hello-cronjob\nspec:\n  schedule: &quot;*/5 * * * *&quot;\n  jobTemplate:\n    spec:\n      template:\n        spec:\n          containers:\n          - name: hello\n            image: alpine:latest\n            command: [&quot;echo&quot;, &quot;Hello&quot;]\n          restartPolicy: OnFailure</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0148","card":"q-kubernetes-043-ingress","sec":"kubernetes-s044","q":"How do you create an Ingress resource?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1\nkind: Ingress\nmetadata:\n  name: my-ingress\nspec:\n  rules:\n  - host: example.com\n    http:\n      paths:\n      - path: /\n        pathType: Prefix\n        backend:\n          service:\n            name: my-service\n            port:\n              number: 80</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0149","card":"q-kubernetes-043-ingress","sec":"kubernetes-s044","q":"How do you route <code>/api</code> to a service with an Ingress?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1\nkind: Ingress\nmetadata:\n  name: api-ingress\nspec:\n  rules:\n  - http:\n      paths:\n      - path: /api\n        pathType: Prefix\n        backend:\n          service:\n            name: api-service\n            port:\n              number: 8080</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0150","card":"q-kubernetes-043-ingress","sec":"kubernetes-s044","q":"How do you configure an Ingress with TLS?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1\nkind: Ingress\nmetadata:\n  name: ingress-tls\nspec:\n  tls:\n  - hosts:\n    - example.com\n    secretName: tls-secret\n  rules:\n  - host: example.com\n    http:\n      paths:\n      - path: /\n        pathType: Prefix\n        backend:\n          service:\n            name: nginx-service\n            port:\n              number: 80</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0151","card":"q-kubernetes-044-namespaces-quotas-and-limits","sec":"kubernetes-s045","q":"How do you create a Namespace?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kubectl create namespace my-namespace</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0152","card":"q-kubernetes-044-namespaces-quotas-and-limits","sec":"kubernetes-s045","q":"How do you create a <code>staging</code> Namespace with the label <code>env=staging</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: v1\nkind: Namespace\nmetadata:\n  name: staging\n  labels:\n    env: staging</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0153","card":"q-kubernetes-044-namespaces-quotas-and-limits","sec":"kubernetes-s045","q":"How do you create a ResourceQuota in a Namespace?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: v1\nkind: ResourceQuota\nmetadata:\n  name: my-resourcequota\n  namespace: my-namespace\nspec:\n  hard:\n    pods: &quot;10&quot;\n    requests.cpu: &quot;2&quot;\n    requests.memory: 4Gi</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0154","card":"q-kubernetes-044-namespaces-quotas-and-limits","sec":"kubernetes-s045","q":"How do you create a LimitRange in a Namespace?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: v1\nkind: LimitRange\nmetadata:\n  name: my-limitrange\n  namespace: my-namespace\nspec:\n  limits:\n  - type: Container\n    default:\n      cpu: &quot;500m&quot;\n      memory: &quot;512Mi&quot;\n    defaultRequest:\n      cpu: &quot;200m&quot;\n      memory: &quot;256Mi&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0155","card":"q-kubernetes-045-autoscaling-and-network-policy","sec":"kubernetes-s046","q":"How do you create a HorizontalPodAutoscaler for a Deployment?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: autoscaling/v2\nkind: HorizontalPodAutoscaler\nmetadata:\n  name: my-hpa\nspec:\n  scaleTargetRef:\n    apiVersion: apps/v1\n    kind: Deployment\n    name: my-deployment\n  minReplicas: 1\n  maxReplicas: 5\n  metrics:\n  - type: Resource\n    resource:\n      name: cpu\n      target:\n        type: Utilization\n        averageUtilization: 50</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0156","card":"q-kubernetes-045-autoscaling-and-network-policy","sec":"kubernetes-s046","q":"How do you create a NetworkPolicy to restrict Pod traffic?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1\nkind: NetworkPolicy\nmetadata:\n  name: my-network-policy\nspec:\n  podSelector:\n    matchLabels:\n      app: nginx\n  policyTypes:\n  - Ingress\n  ingress:\n  - from:\n    - podSelector:\n        matchLabels:\n          app: frontend\n    ports:\n    - protocol: TCP\n      port: 80</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0157","card":"q-kubernetes-046-rbac-and-serviceaccounts","sec":"kubernetes-s047","q":"How do you create a Role and attach it to a ServiceAccount?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1\nkind: Role\nmetadata:\n  name: my-role\n  namespace: default\nrules:\n- apiGroups: [&quot;&quot;]\n  resources: [&quot;pods&quot;]\n  verbs: [&quot;get&quot;, &quot;list&quot;]\n---\napiVersion: v1\nkind: ServiceAccount\nmetadata:\n  name: my-serviceaccount\n  namespace: default\n---\napiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1\nkind: RoleBinding\nmetadata:\n  name: my-role-binding\n  namespace: default\nsubjects:\n- kind: ServiceAccount\n  name: my-serviceaccount\n  namespace: default\nroleRef:\n  kind: Role\n  name: my-role\n  apiGroup: rbac.authorization.k8s.io</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0158","card":"q-kubernetes-046-rbac-and-serviceaccounts","sec":"kubernetes-s047","q":"How do you create a ClusterRole and attach it to a ServiceAccount?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1\nkind: ClusterRole\nmetadata:\n  name: my-clusterrole\nrules:\n- apiGroups: [&quot;&quot;]\n  resources: [&quot;pods&quot;]\n  verbs: [&quot;get&quot;, &quot;list&quot;]\n---\napiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1\nkind: ClusterRoleBinding\nmetadata:\n  name: my-clusterrole-binding\nsubjects:\n- kind: ServiceAccount\n  name: my-serviceaccount\n  namespace: default\nroleRef:\n  kind: ClusterRole\n  name: my-clusterrole\n  apiGroup: rbac.authorization.k8s.io</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0159","card":"q-kubernetes-046-rbac-and-serviceaccounts","sec":"kubernetes-s047","q":"How do you create a ServiceAccount and attach it to a Pod?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: v1\nkind: ServiceAccount\nmetadata:\n  name: my-serviceaccount\n---\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Pod\nmetadata:\n  name: my-pod-with-sa\nspec:\n  serviceAccountName: my-serviceaccount\n  containers:\n  - name: nginx\n    image: nginx</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0160","card":"q-kubernetes-047-listing-logs-and-exec","sec":"kubernetes-s048","q":"How do you list Pods in the <code>default</code> namespace that are Running?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kubectl get pods -n default --field-selector=status.phase=Running</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0161","card":"q-kubernetes-047-listing-logs-and-exec","sec":"kubernetes-s048","q":"How do you check logs of one container in a multi-container Pod?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kubectl logs &lt;pod-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt; -c &lt;container-name&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0162","card":"q-kubernetes-047-listing-logs-and-exec","sec":"kubernetes-s048","q":"How do you exec into <code>app-pod</code> to check processes?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kubectl exec -it app-pod -n &lt;namespace&gt; -- /bin/sh -c &quot;ps aux&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0163","card":"q-kubernetes-047-listing-logs-and-exec","sec":"kubernetes-s048","q":"How do you check Pod events?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kubectl describe pod &lt;pod-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0164","card":"q-kubernetes-047-listing-logs-and-exec","sec":"kubernetes-s048","q":"How do you check Pod CPU and memory usage?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kubectl top pods -n &lt;namespace&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0165","card":"q-kubernetes-048-pending-imagepullbackoff-and-crashloopba","sec":"kubernetes-s049","q":"How do you troubleshoot a Pod stuck in Pending?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kubectl get pod &lt;pod-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt;\nkubectl describe pod &lt;pod-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt;\nkubectl get nodes\nkubectl describe quota -n &lt;namespace&gt;\nkubectl logs -n kube-system -l component=kube-scheduler</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0166","card":"q-kubernetes-048-pending-imagepullbackoff-and-crashloopba","sec":"kubernetes-s049","q":"How do you debug ImagePullBackOff?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kubectl get pod &lt;pod-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt;\nkubectl describe pod &lt;pod-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt;\ndocker pull &lt;image-name:tag&gt;\nkubectl get secret &lt;secret-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0167","card":"q-kubernetes-048-pending-imagepullbackoff-and-crashloopba","sec":"kubernetes-s049","q":"How do you delete Pods in CrashLoopBackOff?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kubectl get pods -n &lt;namespace&gt; -o jsonpath=&#x27;{range .items[*]}{.metadata.name}{&quot;\\t&quot;}{.status.containerStatuses[0].state.waiting.reason}{&quot;\\n&quot;}{end}&#x27; | grep CrashLoopBackOff | awk &#x27;{print $1}&#x27; | xargs kubectl delete pod -n &lt;namespace&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0168","card":"q-kubernetes-048-pending-imagepullbackoff-and-crashloopba","sec":"kubernetes-s049","q":"How do you force delete a Pod stuck in Terminating?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kubectl delete pod &lt;pod-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt; --force --grace-period=0</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0169","card":"q-kubernetes-049-scaling-rollouts-and-patching","sec":"kubernetes-s050","q":"How do you scale the deployment <code>web-app</code> to 5 replicas?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kubectl scale deployment web-app --replicas=5 -n &lt;namespace&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0170","card":"q-kubernetes-049-scaling-rollouts-and-patching","sec":"kubernetes-s050","q":"How do you roll back a deployment to the previous revision?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kubectl rollout undo deployment &lt;deployment-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0171","card":"q-kubernetes-049-scaling-rollouts-and-patching","sec":"kubernetes-s050","q":"How do you investigate a deployment that is not updating?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kubectl get deployment &lt;deployment-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt;\nkubectl describe deployment &lt;deployment-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt;\nkubectl get rs -n &lt;namespace&gt;\nkubectl rollout history deployment &lt;deployment-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt;\nkubectl rollout restart deployment &lt;deployment-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0172","card":"q-kubernetes-049-scaling-rollouts-and-patching","sec":"kubernetes-s050","q":"How do you patch a deployment to add an environment variable?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kubectl patch deployment &lt;deployment-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt; --type=&#x27;json&#x27; -p=&#x27;[{&quot;op&quot;: &quot;add&quot;, &quot;path&quot;: &quot;/spec/template/spec/containers/0/env/-&quot;, &quot;value&quot;: {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;NEW_VAR&quot;, &quot;value&quot;: &quot;new-value&quot;}}]&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0173","card":"q-kubernetes-049-scaling-rollouts-and-patching","sec":"kubernetes-s050","q":"How do you check ReplicaSet status?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kubectl get rs &lt;replicaset-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt;\nkubectl describe rs &lt;replicaset-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0174","card":"q-kubernetes-050-nodes-and-services","sec":"kubernetes-s051","q":"How do you drain a node for maintenance?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kubectl drain &lt;node-name&gt; --ignore-daemonsets --delete-emptydir-data\nkubectl uncordon &lt;node-name&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0175","card":"q-kubernetes-050-nodes-and-services","sec":"kubernetes-s051","q":"How do you cordon a node and reschedule its Pods?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kubectl cordon &lt;node-name&gt;\nkubectl drain &lt;node-name&gt; --ignore-daemonsets --delete-emptydir-data</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0176","card":"q-kubernetes-050-nodes-and-services","sec":"kubernetes-s051","q":"How do you taint a node to block Pods?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kubectl taint nodes &lt;node-name&gt; key=value:NoSchedule</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0177","card":"q-kubernetes-050-nodes-and-services","sec":"kubernetes-s051","q":"How do you describe a service and check its endpoints?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kubectl describe service &lt;service-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt;\nkubectl get endpoints &lt;service-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0178","card":"q-kubernetes-051-ansible-tasks-that-drive-kubectl","sec":"kubernetes-s052","q":"How do you use Ansible to apply a Kubernetes manifest and verify it?","a":"<p>Apply <code>pod.yaml</code>, read the phase with jsonpath, and fail the play if the Pod is not Running.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Apply K8s\n  hosts: localhost\n  tasks:\n  - name: Apply\n    ansible.builtin.command: kubectl apply -f pod.yaml\n  - name: Verify\n    ansible.builtin.command: kubectl get pod nginx-pod -o jsonpath=&#x27;{.status.phase}&#x27;\n    register: pod_status\n  - name: Fail if not running\n    ansible.builtin.fail: { msg: &quot;Pod not Running&quot; }\n    when: pod_status.stdout != &quot;Running&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0179","card":"q-kubernetes-051-ansible-tasks-that-drive-kubectl","sec":"kubernetes-s052","q":"How do you use Ansible to install <code>kubectl</code> and check the cluster?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Install kubectl\n  hosts: all\n  become: yes\n  tasks:\n  - name: Install\n    ansible.builtin.shell: |\n      curl -LO &quot;https://dl.k8s.io/release/$(curl -L -s https://dl.k8s.io/release/stable.txt)/bin/linux/amd64/kubectl&quot;\n      chmod +x kubectl &amp;&amp; mv kubectl /usr/local/bin/\n    args: { creates: /usr/local/bin/kubectl }\n  - name: Check cluster\n    ansible.builtin.command: kubectl cluster-info\n    register: cluster_info\n  - name: Debug\n    ansible.builtin.debug: { var: cluster_info.stdout }</code></pre></div>\n<p>Run it with <code>ansible-playbook install_kubectl.yml</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0180","card":"q-kubernetes-051-ansible-tasks-that-drive-kubectl","sec":"kubernetes-s052","q":"How do you use Ansible to update a ConfigMap and restart the Pods?","a":"<p>Apply <code>configmap.yaml</code>, then restart the Deployment.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Update ConfigMap\n  hosts: localhost\n  tasks:\n  - name: Apply\n    ansible.builtin.command: kubectl apply -f configmap.yaml\n  - name: Restart\n    ansible.builtin.command: kubectl rollout restart deployment web-app -n default</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0181","card":"q-kubernetes-052-checking-logs-and-exposing-services-with","sec":"kubernetes-s053","q":"How do you check Pod logs with Ansible and fail on errors?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Check logs\n  hosts: localhost\n  tasks:\n  - name: Get logs\n    ansible.builtin.command: kubectl logs &lt;pod-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt;\n    register: pod_logs\n  - name: Fail on error\n    ansible.builtin.fail: { msg: &quot;Errors in logs&quot; }\n    when: &quot;&#x27;error&#x27; in pod_logs.stdout | lower&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0182","card":"q-kubernetes-052-checking-logs-and-exposing-services-with","sec":"kubernetes-s053","q":"How do you use Ansible to deploy a Service and expose it externally?","a":"<p>Apply a ClusterIP Service (<code>port: 80</code>, <code>targetPort: 8080</code>), then expose it as a LoadBalancer.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Deploy service\n  hosts: localhost\n  tasks:\n  - name: Apply\n    ansible.builtin.command: kubectl apply -f service.yaml\n  - name: Expose\n    ansible.builtin.command: kubectl expose service web-service --type=LoadBalancer --port=80 --name=web-lb -n default</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0183","card":"q-kubernetes-052-checking-logs-and-exposing-services-with","sec":"kubernetes-s053","q":"How do you troubleshoot an Ansible-deployed Pod that is not running?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kubectl get pod &lt;pod-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt;\nkubectl describe pod &lt;pod-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt;\nkubectl logs &lt;pod-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt;\nkubectl get pod &lt;pod-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt; -o yaml</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0184","card":"q-kubernetes-053-github-actions-workflows-that-run-kubect","sec":"kubernetes-s054","q":"How do you scale a Kubernetes deployment from GitHub Actions on a version tag?","a":"<p>Write the kubeconfig from a secret, then run <code>kubectl scale</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>name: Scale K8s\non: { push: { tags: [&#x27;v*&#x27;] } }\njobs:\n  scale:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n    - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n    - uses: azure/setup-kubectl@v3\n    - run: echo &quot;${{ secrets.KUBECONFIG }}&quot; &gt; $HOME/.kube/config\n    - run: kubectl scale deployment web-app --replicas=5 -n default</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0185","card":"q-kubernetes-053-github-actions-workflows-that-run-kubect","sec":"kubernetes-s054","q":"How do you restart a rollout from GitHub Actions when config changes?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>name: Restart Deployment\non: { push: { branches: [main], paths: [&#x27;config/*&#x27;] } }\njobs:\n  restart:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n    - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n    - uses: azure/setup-kubectl@v3\n    - run: echo &quot;${{ secrets.KUBECONFIG }}&quot; &gt; $HOME/.kube/config\n    - run: kubectl apply -f config/configmap.yaml\n    - run: kubectl rollout restart deployment web-app -n default</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0186","card":"q-kubernetes-054-configuring-nodes-with-ansible-and-githu","sec":"kubernetes-s055","q":"How do you use GitHub Actions with Ansible to configure a Kubernetes node and verify it?","a":"<p>The workflow installs Ansible, runs the playbook, then lists nodes with <code>kubectl</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>name: Configure Node\non: { push: { branches: [main] } }\njobs:\n  configure:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n    - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n    - run: sudo apt update &amp;&amp; sudo apt install -y ansible\n    - run: ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini configure_node.yml\n    - uses: azure/setup-kubectl@v3\n    - run: echo &quot;${{ secrets.KUBECONFIG }}&quot; &gt; $HOME/.kube/config\n    - run: kubectl get nodes</code></pre></div>\n<p>The playbook <code>configure_node.yml</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Configure node\n  hosts: k8s_nodes\n  become: yes\n  tasks:\n  - name: Install kubeadm\n    ansible.builtin.package: { name: kubeadm, state: present }</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0187","card":"q-kubernetes-055-why-use-python-for-kubernetes","sec":"kubernetes-s056","q":"What are the benefits of using Python to automate Kubernetes resource management?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Rich libraries</strong>: the <code>kubernetes</code> Python client simplifies API interactions for pods, services, and deployments.</li>\n  <li><strong>Flexibility</strong>: scripts can handle complex logic, error handling, and integrations with other tools.</li>\n  <li><strong>Community support</strong>: extensive documentation and community-driven tools.</li>\n  <li><strong>Portability</strong>: Python scripts work across environments.</li>\n  <li><strong>Automation</strong>: repetitive tasks like scaling, monitoring, and updating resources can be scripted.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0188","card":"q-kubernetes-055-why-use-python-for-kubernetes","sec":"kubernetes-s056","q":"What are the challenges of managing multi-cloud resources (for example AWS and Kubernetes) with Python?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Complexity</strong>: each API has its own nuances.</li>\n  <li><strong>Authentication</strong>: different credential mechanisms (AWS IAM vs Kubernetes RBAC).</li>\n  <li><strong>State management</strong>: reconciling states across clouds (Terraform state vs Kubernetes resources).</li>\n  <li><strong>Error handling</strong>: varied error formats and retry policies.</li>\n  <li><strong>Dependencies</strong>: library versions and compatibility.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0189","card":"q-kubernetes-055-why-use-python-for-kubernetes","sec":"kubernetes-s056","q":"How can Python be used to interact with the Kubernetes API for cluster management?","a":"<p>The <code>kubernetes</code> client supports CRUD operations on resources, watching resource changes, and executing commands in pods.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from kubernetes import client, config\nconfig.load_kube_config()\nv1 = client.CoreV1Api()\npods = v1.list_pod_for_all_namespaces()\nfor pod in pods.items:\n    print(f&quot;Pod: {pod.metadata.name}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0190","card":"q-kubernetes-056-authenticating-and-listing-pods","sec":"kubernetes-s057","q":"How do you authenticate a Python script to a Kubernetes cluster's API?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Kubeconfig file</strong>: <code>config.load_kube_config()</code> reads <code>~/.kube/config</code>.</li>\n  <li><strong>In-cluster config</strong>: inside a Pod, use <code>config.load_incluster_config()</code> with a service account token.</li>\n  <li><strong>Manual token</strong>: provide a bearer token and cluster URL explicitly.</li>\n  <li><strong>Certificates</strong>: use client certificates.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>In-cluster example:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from kubernetes import client, config\n# Assumes running in a pod with a service account\nconfig.load_incluster_config()\nv1 = client.CoreV1Api()\npods = v1.list_pod_for_all_namespaces()\nfor pod in pods.items:\n    print(f&quot;Pod: {pod.metadata.name}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0191","card":"q-kubernetes-056-authenticating-and-listing-pods","sec":"kubernetes-s057","q":"How do you list all Pods in a namespace with the <code>kubernetes</code> client?","a":"<p>Use <code>CoreV1Api.list_namespaced_pod</code>. Configure credentials with a kubeconfig or service account token.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from kubernetes import client, config\n# Use config.load_incluster_config() when running in a cluster\nconfig.load_kube_config()\nv1 = client.CoreV1Api()\nnamespace = &quot;default&quot;\npods = v1.list_namespaced_pod(namespace=namespace)\nfor pod in pods.items:\n    print(f&quot;Pod: {pod.metadata.name}, Status: {pod.status.phase}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0192","card":"q-kubernetes-057-creating-and-scaling-deployments","sec":"kubernetes-s058","q":"How do you deploy a Kubernetes Deployment with the <code>kubernetes</code> client?","a":"<p>Build a <code>V1Deployment</code> and create it with <code>AppsV1Api</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from kubernetes import client, config\nconfig.load_kube_config()\napps_v1 = client.AppsV1Api()\ndeployment = client.V1Deployment(\n    metadata=client.V1ObjectMeta(name=&quot;nginx-deployment&quot;),\n    spec=client.V1DeploymentSpec(\n        replicas=3,\n        selector=client.V1LabelSelector(match_labels={&quot;app&quot;: &quot;nginx&quot;}),\n        template=client.V1PodTemplateSpec(\n            metadata=client.V1ObjectMeta(labels={&quot;app&quot;: &quot;nginx&quot;}),\n            spec=client.V1PodSpec(\n                containers=[\n                    client.V1Container(\n                        name=&quot;nginx&quot;,\n                        image=&quot;nginx:latest&quot;,\n                        ports=[client.V1ContainerPort(container_port=80)]\n                    )\n                ]\n            )\n        )\n    )\n)\nnamespace = &quot;default&quot;\napps_v1.create_namespaced_deployment(namespace=namespace, body=deployment)\nprint(&quot;Deployment created successfully&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0193","card":"q-kubernetes-057-creating-and-scaling-deployments","sec":"kubernetes-s058","q":"How do you scale a Deployment programmatically?","a":"<p>Use <code>AppsV1Api.patch_namespaced_deployment_scale</code> with the deployment name and namespace.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from kubernetes import client, config\nconfig.load_kube_config()\napps_v1 = client.AppsV1Api()\nnamespace = &quot;default&quot;\ndeployment_name = &quot;nginx-deployment&quot;\nreplicas = 5\nscale = client.V1Scale(\n    metadata=client.V1ObjectMeta(name=deployment_name, namespace=namespace),\n    spec=client.V1ScaleSpec(replicas=replicas)\n)\napps_v1.patch_namespaced_deployment_scale(\n    name=deployment_name,\n    namespace=namespace,\n    body=scale\n)\nprint(f&quot;Scaled {deployment_name} to {replicas} replicas&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0194","card":"q-kubernetes-058-configmaps-and-services","sec":"kubernetes-s059","q":"How do you create a ConfigMap with the <code>kubernetes</code> client?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from kubernetes import client, config\nconfig.load_kube_config()\nv1 = client.CoreV1Api()\nconfig_map = client.V1ConfigMap(\n    metadata=client.V1ObjectMeta(name=&quot;my-configmap&quot;),\n    data={\n        &quot;database_url&quot;: &quot;mysql://user:pass@localhost:3306/db&quot;,\n        &quot;log_level&quot;: &quot;DEBUG&quot;\n    }\n)\nnamespace = &quot;default&quot;\nv1.create_namespaced_config_map(namespace=namespace, body=config_map)\nprint(&quot;ConfigMap created successfully&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0195","card":"q-kubernetes-058-configmaps-and-services","sec":"kubernetes-s059","q":"How do you delete a Service with the <code>kubernetes</code> client?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from kubernetes import client, config\nconfig.load_kube_config()\nv1 = client.CoreV1Api()\nnamespace = &quot;default&quot;\nservice_name = &quot;my-service&quot;\nv1.delete_namespaced_service(name=service_name, namespace=namespace)\nprint(f&quot;Service {service_name} deleted successfully&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0196","card":"q-kubernetes-059-events-errors-and-rbac","sec":"kubernetes-s060","q":"How do you monitor Kubernetes events with Python?","a":"<p>Call <code>list_namespaced_event</code>, or open a watch stream with <code>watch.Watch</code> for real-time events.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from kubernetes import client, config, watch\nconfig.load_kube_config()\nv1 = client.CoreV1Api()\nnamespace = &quot;default&quot;\nw = watch.Watch()\nfor event in w.stream(v1.list_namespaced_event, namespace=namespace):\n    evt = event[&#x27;object&#x27;]\n    print(f&quot;Event: {evt.type}, Reason: {evt.reason}, Message: {evt.message}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0197","card":"q-kubernetes-059-events-errors-and-rbac","sec":"kubernetes-s060","q":"How do you handle Kubernetes API errors in Python?","a":"<p>Catch <code>ApiException</code> and check the status code and reason (404 not found, 403 unauthorized).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from kubernetes import client, config\nfrom kubernetes.client.rest import ApiException\nconfig.load_kube_config()\nv1 = client.CoreV1Api()\ntry:\n    namespace = &quot;default&quot;\n    pod_name = &quot;non-existent-pod&quot;\n    v1.read_namespaced_pod(name=pod_name, namespace=namespace)\nexcept ApiException as e:\n    if e.status == 404:\n        print(f&quot;Pod {pod_name} not found&quot;)\n    elif e.status == 403:\n        print(&quot;Permission denied&quot;)\n    else:\n        print(f&quot;Error: {e}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0198","card":"q-kubernetes-059-events-errors-and-rbac","sec":"kubernetes-s060","q":"How do you manage Kubernetes RBAC policies with Python?","a":"<p>Use <code>RbacAuthorizationV1Api</code> to create, update, or delete <code>Role</code>, <code>RoleBinding</code>, <code>ClusterRole</code>, and <code>ClusterRoleBinding</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from kubernetes import client, config\nconfig.load_kube_config()\nrbac_v1 = client.RbacAuthorizationV1Api()\nrole = client.V1Role(\n    metadata=client.V1ObjectMeta(name=&quot;pod-reader&quot;),\n    rules=[\n        client.V1PolicyRule(\n            api_groups=[&quot;&quot;],\n            resources=[&quot;pods&quot;],\n            verbs=[&quot;get&quot;, &quot;list&quot;, &quot;watch&quot;]\n        )\n    ]\n)\nnamespace = &quot;default&quot;\nrbac_v1.create_namespaced_role(namespace=namespace, body=role)\nrole_binding = client.V1RoleBinding(\n    metadata=client.V1ObjectMeta(name=&quot;pod-reader-binding&quot;),\n    subjects=[\n        client.V1Subject(kind=&quot;User&quot;, name=&quot;jane&quot;, api_group=&quot;rbac.authorization.k8s.io&quot;)\n    ],\n    role_ref=client.V1RoleRef(\n        kind=&quot;Role&quot;,\n        name=&quot;pod-reader&quot;,\n        api_group=&quot;rbac.authorization.k8s.io&quot;\n    )\n)\nrbac_v1.create_namespaced_role_binding(namespace=namespace, body=role_binding)\nprint(&quot;Role and RoleBinding created successfully&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0199","card":"q-kubernetes-060-operators-and-custom-controllers","sec":"kubernetes-s061","q":"What is a Kubernetes operator, and how can Python create one?","a":"<p>An operator is a custom controller that extends Kubernetes to manage complex applications. It uses custom resources and controllers to automate tasks like scaling or backups. In Python, use <code>kopf</code> (Kubernetes Operator Pythonic Framework) or the <code>kubernetes</code> client to define custom resources (CRDs), reconcile desired and actual state, and deploy the operator as a Pod in the cluster.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0200","card":"q-kubernetes-060-operators-and-custom-controllers","sec":"kubernetes-s061","q":"How can Python create a custom Kubernetes controller?","a":"<p>A controller watches changes to custom resources and reconciles the desired state. Use the <code>kubernetes</code> client with <code>watch.Watch</code> to monitor CRDs, or use <code>kopf</code> or <code>operator-sdk</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import kopf\nfrom kubernetes import client, config\nconfig.load_kube_config()\n\n@kopf.on.create(&#x27;example.com&#x27;, &#x27;v1&#x27;, &#x27;myresources&#x27;)\ndef create_fn(spec, name, namespace, **kwargs):\n    print(f&quot;Creating resource {name} in namespace {namespace}&quot;)\n    # Add logic to reconcile the resource\n    return {&#x27;message&#x27;: &#x27;Resource created&#x27;}\n\n@kopf.on.update(&#x27;example.com&#x27;, &#x27;v1&#x27;, &#x27;myresources&#x27;)\ndef update_fn(spec, name, namespace, **kwargs):\n    print(f&quot;Updating resource {name} in namespace {namespace}&quot;)\n    # Add logic to update the resource</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0201","card":"q-kubernetes-060-operators-and-custom-controllers","sec":"kubernetes-s061","q":"A Python operator is not responding to custom resource events. How do you troubleshoot it?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Check logs</strong>: inspect operator logs for errors.</li>\n  <li><strong>Verify RBAC</strong>: the operator needs permission to watch custom resources.</li>\n  <li><strong>Test event handling</strong>: simulate events to verify the handler.</li>\n  <li><strong>Debug code</strong>: add logging to the event loop.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from kubernetes import client, config, watch\nimport logging\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO)\n\ndef watch_custom_resources(namespace, group, version, plural):\n    config.load_kube_config()\n    custom_api = client.CustomObjectsApi()\n    w = watch.Watch()\n    for event in w.stream(custom_api.list_namespaced_custom_object, group, version, namespace, plural):\n        logging.info(f&quot;Event: {event[&#x27;type&#x27;]}, Object: {event[&#x27;object&#x27;][&#x27;metadata&#x27;][&#x27;name&#x27;]}&quot;)\n        # Add event handling logic here\n\nwatch_custom_resources(&quot;default&quot;, &quot;example.com&quot;, &quot;v1&quot;, &quot;myresources&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0202","card":"q-kubernetes-061-python-troubleshooting-scenarios","sec":"kubernetes-s062","q":"A Pod is failing because of a misconfigured ConfigMap. How do you diagnose and fix it with Python?","a":"<p>Inspect the Pod status, read the ConfigMap, and update it if a key is missing.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from kubernetes import client, config\n\ndef fix_configmap(namespace, pod_name, configmap_name):\n    config.load_kube_config()  # Or load_incluster_config() in a cluster\n    v1 = client.CoreV1Api()\n    pod = v1.read_namespaced_pod(pod_name, namespace)\n    if pod.status.phase != &quot;Running&quot;:\n        print(f&quot;Pod {pod_name} is not running: {pod.status.phase}&quot;)\n        for container_status in pod.status.container_statuses:\n            if container_status.state.terminated:\n                print(f&quot;Exit code: {container_status.state.terminated.exit_code}&quot;)\n    configmap = v1.read_namespaced_config_map(configmap_name, namespace)\n    if &quot;required_key&quot; not in configmap.data:\n        configmap.data[&quot;required_key&quot;] = &quot;required_value&quot;\n        v1.replace_namespaced_config_map(configmap_name, namespace, configmap)\n        print(f&quot;Updated ConfigMap {configmap_name}&quot;)\n\nfix_configmap(&quot;default&quot;, &quot;my-pod&quot;, &quot;my-configmap&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0203","card":"q-kubernetes-061-python-troubleshooting-scenarios","sec":"kubernetes-s062","q":"An Ansible playbook is failing on certain Kubernetes nodes because of network issues. How do you diagnose it with Python?","a":"<p>Check node status with the <code>kubernetes</code> client and verify network configuration (VPC, security groups) with <code>boto3</code>. Restart or replace the problematic nodes.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from kubernetes import client, config\nimport boto3\n\ndef diagnose_k8s_nodes(namespace):\n    config.load_kube_config()\n    v1 = client.CoreV1Api()\n    nodes = v1.list_node()\n    for node in nodes.items:\n        for condition in node.status.conditions:\n            if condition.type == &quot;NetworkUnavailable&quot; and condition.status == &quot;True&quot;:\n                print(f&quot;Node {node.metadata.name} has network issues&quot;)\n                ec2 = boto3.client(&quot;ec2&quot;)\n                response = ec2.describe_instances(Filters=[{&quot;Name&quot;: &quot;private-dns-name&quot;, &quot;Values&quot;: [node.metadata.name]}])\n                instance_id = response[&quot;Reservations&quot;][0][&quot;Instances&quot;][0][&quot;InstanceId&quot;]\n                ec2.reboot_instances(InstanceIds=[instance_id])\n                print(f&quot;Rebooted node {node.metadata.name}&quot;)\n\ndiagnose_k8s_nodes(&quot;default&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0204","card":"q-kubernetes-062-python-autoscaling-and-resource-analysis","sec":"kubernetes-s063","q":"How do you scale a deployment on CPU usage with Python and the Kubernetes API?","a":"<p>Read CPU usage from the Metrics API and scale with the AppsV1 API.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from kubernetes import client, config\nimport time\n\ndef scale_deployment(namespace, deployment_name, cpu_threshold=70, max_replicas=10):\n    config.load_kube_config()\n    apps_v1 = client.AppsV1Api()\n    metrics_api = client.CustomObjectsApi()\n    while True:\n        deployment = apps_v1.read_namespaced_deployment(deployment_name, namespace)\n        current_replicas = deployment.spec.replicas\n        metrics = metrics_api.list_namespaced_custom_object(\n            group=&quot;metrics.k8s.io&quot;, version=&quot;v1beta1&quot;, namespace=namespace, plural=&quot;pods&quot;\n        )\n        cpu_usage = 0\n        for item in metrics[&quot;items&quot;]:\n            if item[&quot;metadata&quot;][&quot;name&quot;].startswith(deployment_name):\n                cpu_usage += sum(int(c[&quot;usage&quot;][&quot;cpu&quot;].rstrip(&quot;n&quot;)) for c in item[&quot;containers&quot;])\n        if cpu_usage &gt; cpu_threshold and current_replicas &lt; max_replicas:\n            new_replicas = min(current_replicas + 1, max_replicas)\n            deployment.spec.replicas = new_replicas\n            apps_v1.patch_namespaced_deployment(deployment_name, namespace, deployment)\n            print(f&quot;Scaled up to {new_replicas} replicas&quot;)\n        elif cpu_usage &lt; cpu_threshold / 2 and current_replicas &gt; 1:\n            new_replicas = max(current_replicas - 1, 1)\n            deployment.spec.replicas = new_replicas\n            apps_v1.patch_namespaced_deployment(deployment_name, namespace, deployment)\n            print(f&quot;Scaled down to {new_replicas} replicas&quot;)\n        time.sleep(60)\n\nscale_deployment(&quot;default&quot;, &quot;my-deployment&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0205","card":"q-kubernetes-063-analyzing-resource-usage-with-python","sec":"kubernetes-s064","q":"A cluster is running out of resources. How do you analyze usage with Python and suggest optimizations?","a":"<p>Use the <code>kubernetes</code> client and Metrics API to compare usage with limits.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from kubernetes import client, config\n\ndef analyze_k8s_resources(namespace):\n    config.load_kube_config()\n    v1 = client.CoreV1Api()\n    metrics_api = client.CustomObjectsApi()\n    pods = v1.list_namespaced_pod(namespace)\n    for pod in pods.items:\n        metrics = metrics_api.get_namespaced_custom_object(\n            group=&quot;metrics.k8s.io&quot;, version=&quot;v1beta1&quot;, namespace=namespace, plural=&quot;pods&quot;, name=pod.metadata.name\n        )\n        for container in metrics[&quot;containers&quot;]:\n            cpu = container[&quot;usage&quot;][&quot;cpu&quot;].rstrip(&quot;n&quot;)\n            memory = container[&quot;usage&quot;][&quot;memory&quot;].rstrip(&quot;Ki&quot;)\n            print(f&quot;Pod: {pod.metadata.name}, Container: {container[&#x27;name&#x27;]}, CPU: {cpu}n, Memory: {memory}Ki&quot;)\n            if int(cpu) &gt; 500:  # Example threshold\n                print(f&quot;Recommendation: Reduce CPU limit for {container[&#x27;name&#x27;]}&quot;)\n\nanalyze_k8s_resources(&quot;default&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"kubernetes-f0206","card":"q-kubernetes-063-analyzing-resource-usage-with-python","sec":"kubernetes-s064","q":"A Python script calling the Kubernetes API is timing out on a large cluster. How do you optimize it?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Use pagination</strong>: limit results with <code>limit</code> and <code>continue</code>.</li>\n  <li><strong>Increase the timeout</strong>: adjust the HTTP client timeout.</li>\n  <li><strong>Cache results</strong>: store frequently accessed data locally.</li>\n  <li><strong>Parallelize requests</strong>: use <code>concurrent.futures</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from kubernetes import client, config\n\ndef list_pods_optimized(namespace):\n    config.load_kube_config()\n    v1 = client.CoreV1Api()\n    pods = []\n    limit = 100\n    continue_token = None\n    while True:\n        response = v1.list_namespaced_pod(namespace, limit=limit, _continue=continue_token)\n        pods.extend(response.items)\n        continue_token = response.metadata._continue\n        if not continue_token:\n            break\n    for pod in pods:\n        print(f&quot;Pod: {pod.metadata.name}&quot;)\n\nlist_pods_optimized(&quot;default&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false}];
